          "text": "{\"issues\":[{\"seed\":123,\"severity\":\"major\",\"layer\":\"prose\",\"defect\":\"contradiction\",\"evidence\":\"After Juniper climbs and the trace keeps Lila and Tomas at `foot`, the ending says, “Juniper laughed at the top, while Lila waved from the path below,” despite the immediately preceding hilltop feast with Lila pouring fizz there.\",\"fix\":\"Keep Lila at the hilltop through the feast and ending, or add a traced/textual return down the path before she waves.\"},{\"seed\":791,\"severity\":\"major\",\"layer\":\"prose\",\"defect\":\"wrong_knowledge\",\"evidence\":\"The opening states that Juniper has “a very particular wish: quiet, please,” but no event gives Lila—or anyone—knowledge of `juniper.wish`, which remains null throughout the trace.\",\"fix\":\"Either add an event in which Juniper tells Lila her wish, or narrate the wish from Juniper’s own explicit speech rather than as ungrounded character knowledge.\"},{\"seed\":791,\"severity\":\"major\",\"layer\":\"prose\",\"defect\":\"contradiction\",\"evidence\":\"Juniper’s traced wish is `quiet`, yet the story resolves it with “bell answered, ding!” and a “bell chiming” procession followed by Tomas clapping, without any turn that accommodates or revises her request.\",\"fix\":\"Replace the noisy procession with a quiet celebration, or include a consequential choice to silence/remove the bell and ask for quiet applause.\"}],\"strengths\":\"Seeds 457 and 791 accurately realize the traced loading, crown/bell transfer, Moss’s agreement, procession, and completed foot-side picnic; seed 123 also closely follows its knowledge, invitation, climb, bell, and fizz events.\"}",
